---
title: "duplication_grouping (Sherlock Watsons)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_target: select target issue
    q_get_target --> q_get_candidate: evaluate potential duplicate
    q_get_candidate --> q_check_root_cause: does candidate identify same root cause?
    q_check_root_cause --> q_rc_yes: root cause identified
    q_check_root_cause --> q_rc_no: root cause not identified
    q_rc_no --> q_not_dup: not a duplicate (judge independently)
    q_rc_yes --> q_check_impact: does candidate identify >= Medium impact?
    q_check_impact --> q_impact_yes: medium or high impact identified
    q_check_impact --> q_impact_no: impact below medium
    q_impact_no --> q_not_dup: not a duplicate (judge independently)
    q_impact_yes --> q_check_path: does candidate identify valid attack/vulnerability path?
    q_check_path --> q_path_yes: valid path identified
    q_check_path --> q_path_no: no valid path
    q_path_no --> q_not_dup: not a duplicate (judge independently)
    q_path_yes --> q_is_dup: confirmed duplicate
    q_is_dup --> q_assign_severity: all duplicates awarded highest severity in group
    q_assign_severity --> [*]: duplication resolved
    q_not_dup --> q_solo_judge: judge as solo/different issue/invalid
    q_solo_judge --> [*]: independent judgment

    note right of q_check_root_cause
        INV-001: Three requirements for duplication: root cause + medium impact + valid path
        INV-002: All three must be met simultaneously
    end note

    note right of q_rc_yes
        INV-003: Same root cause categories - same logic mistake across contracts
        INV-004: Same conceptual mistake (e.g. untrusted admin stealing funds)
        INV-005: Category-based grouping: slippage, reentrancy, access control, front-run/sandwich
    end note

    note right of q_assign_severity
        INV-006: All duplicates awarded the highest severity found among the group
        INV-007: Different code implementations/impacts/fixes may split into separate groups
    end note
